{
  "schema": "trueopen-parser-tool-call-v1",
  "source": "docs/TOOL_CALL_PARSER_V1.md, hermes@1",
  "parser": "hermes@1",
  "notes": [
    "input_utf8 is committed output (or, for a tool-call file, the tool stage's input). Positions, splits and matching are on its UTF-8 bytes.",
    "finish_reason, when present, is the verified finish reason from the signed Fin (TRUEOPEN_OUTPUT_FIN_V1), written as its FinishReasonV1 enum name. Absent means no verified finish reason.",
    "stream_splits lists frame boundaries as byte offsets into input_utf8; each list cuts the input into frames at those offsets, and feeding the frames in order must give exactly expected. A boundary may fall inside a marker or inside a multi-byte UTF-8 sequence.",
    "tool_calls compares name and arguments only, byte for byte; id, type and index are synthesised by the Provider and are not part of the vectors.",
    "reasoning_parser \"unsupported@1\" names a reserved reasoning parser that no SDK supports, to exercise the Support rule."
  ],
  "vectors": [
